// A call that passes a struct of 600 words by value puts about 4.7 KiB
// of stack arguments below the frame, so the $OUT slot of the runtime
// calls returning a Str through a length pointer (obj.xo's
// rs_push_byte export, a BytesBuilder's write_byte; rs_push_rune until
// it moved to Xo on 2026-10-15, str_repeat and str_slice_at until they
// moved to Xo in 2026-10, str_replace until decision 0193) is past the 4095 byte immediate of
// `add`; the arm64 backend materializes its address with a shifted add
// (gotchas/arm64-add-immediate-range.md). Found by the self hosted SSA
// builder (decision 0150), whose Builder is that large. Since decision
// 0151 only calls through function values pass such a struct as words.

